<h2>Measurement details</h2>

<p>
  <strong>Cold</strong> starts a new CLI process for every run without a persistent checker result
  cache. <strong>Warm</strong> also starts a new process, but checks the unchanged file using Basilisk&rsquo;s
  or mypy&rsquo;s persistent cache. Warm results are measured only for those two tools and are not editor
  or LSP latency.
</p>

<p>
  <a href="https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine">Hyperfine</a> runs each command twice before timing,
  then records at least {{ benchmarks.meta.runsCount }} measured runs per file. Every tool receives the
  same config-neutral copy of the linked fixture. mypy runs in strict, non-incremental mode for the
  cold measurement; zuban runs in strict mypy mode with its cache cleared. A dash means the tool was
  unavailable or failed the untimed preflight for that file.
</p>

<p>
  These are synthetic, single-file CLI measurements, not per-rule costs, multi-file project throughput,
  or incremental editor latency. See the
  <a href="{{ site.github }}/blob/main/benchmarks/run.sh">benchmark runner</a> for the exact commands,
  or reproduce the table with <code>make bench</code>.
</p>
